            },
            "hypothesis": "Unrolling the outer i-loop by a factor of two (pairwise computation) and fusing the inner j-loops for consecutive bodies improves memory locality because each load of body j's coordinates is reused for both i and i+1, reducing cache misses. This transformation preserves exact floating-point accumulation order per body since each body still sums over all j sequentially; only the interleaving of loads changes. Combined with SoA layout and OpenMP parallelism, this should further reduce memory traffic without altering correctness.",
